        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1101">

                <pb facs="1133" n="1013" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg1013"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Bowen to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-01-11"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 11,
                    1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Bowen states that the protocol should define what are diplomatic questions,
                    as Venezuela often claims questions before her courts are not diplomatic; that
                    provision should be made to prevent delays <pb facs="1134" n="1014"
                        xml:id="pg1014"/> in choosing arbitrators and having them sit and render
                    decisions; that Bermudez case ought to go to The Hague, and that custom-houses
                    should remain guarantee, with power of substituting Americans for Belgians with
                    consent of other creditors. He thinks disputes about interpretation of the
                    protocol should be referred to the President of the United States.</p>
                <p>He adds that it will be very difficult to induce President of Venezuela to make
                    protocol unless he sees we are ready to use force.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
